<title>JAPAN: Japan July domestic vehicle sales fall 10.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Japan July domestic vehicle sales fall 10.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's domestic vehicle sales fell 10.1 percent  in July from a year earlier to 471,623 units, the Japan Automobile  Dealers' Association (JADA) said on Friday.</p>
<p>It was the fourth straight month in which domestic sales had fallen  on a year-on-year basis.  </p>
<p>The July sales breakdown was as follows (with percentage</p>
<p>changes from a year earlier):</p>
<p> Total cars		325,488  down 11.4 percent</p>
<p> - Cars over 2001 cc    75,150  down  6.9 percent</p>
<p> - Cars under 2000 cc  250,338  down 12.7 percent</p>
<p> Trucks		    144,809  down  6.8 percent</p>
<p> - Heavy trucks	   11,626  down 10.9 percent</p>
<p> - Light trucks	  133,183  down  6.4 percent</p>
<p> Buses			 1,326  down 15.3 percent</p>
<p>July sales included 31,353 imported vehicles, down 25.6 percent from  a year before.</p>
<p>July vehicle sales by five major Japanese makers were as</p>
<p>follows (with percentage changes from a year earlier):</p>
<p> Toyota Motor     185,056  down  9.1 percent</p>
<p> Nissan Motor     104,433  down 13.0 percent</p>
<p> Honda Motor	 42,613  down 11.6 percent</p>
<p> Mitsubishi Motors 40,304  down  7.4 percent</p>
<p> Mazda Motor	 25,828  down  0.6 percent</p>
</text>
